  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Vision School Health and Hygiene Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Vision aims to distribute approximately 550 reusable sanitary kits in 3 target schools, with approximately 1,650 underwear for girls. World Vision will engage with the Provincial Education Sector and the school leadership of the 3 target schools to obtain consent for conducting advocacy and awareness-raising session on Menstrual Hygiene Management (MHM).M&amp;J Enterprise, a locally owned and operated company, will be contracted to provide Menstrual hygiene and Management advocacy and awareness to the students and staff of each target schools. The project will be paying M&amp;J Enterprises a consultancy fee of $1000 per day, and three staff from M&amp;J Enterprise will be conducting the sessions for the boys, girls and staff, alongside World Vision.</narrative>
  </description>
